"cups-11|pentacles-12":"A gentle impulse is paired with slow, dependable effort; feeling shows its worth by turning up again, quietly and on time, not just once.",
"cups-11|pentacles-13":"Tenderness learns practical care: the feeling matters most when it shows up as a made meal, a small favor, or a capable hand at the right moment.",
"cups-11|pentacles-14":"A soft new sentiment gets a steady, well-provided setting to grow in; emotion feels safer when the material ground under it is handled competently.",
"cups-12|cups-13":"A romantic offer meets someone whose feelings run deep and steady; charm is welcome, but it will be measured against the quieter proof of consistency.",
"cups-12|cups-14":"An eager invitation of the heart meets emotion that has learned restraint; the gesture lands best when sincerity is matched by mature, kindly judgement.",
"cups-12|swords-01":"A romantic gesture meets a sudden, clear thought; the invitation deserves an honest answer, and clarity is a kindness to everyone involved.",
"cups-12|swords-02":"An invitation arrives while you hold yourself in a careful stalemate; the heart leans forward and the mind keeps its eyes covered, so one has to give.",
"cups-12|swords-03":"Right on a tender bruise lands the offer of romance; acknowledge the hurt out loud before you decide whether this gesture can be received with an open hand.",
"cups-12|swords-04":"An invitation can wait while you rest; a heart that is weary of its own storms answers better after quiet than in the middle of the noise.",
"cups-12|swords-05":"A charming gesture sits beside a sour contest; check whether the offer is sincere or whether someone just wants to be seen winning the room.",
"cups-12|swords-06":"Just as you move toward calmer water, romance extends its hand; take the offer only if it travels well, and does not drag the old turbulence along.",
"cups-12|swords-07":"A gesture that looks generous may hide an angle; ask what the invitation is really for, and trust what the details tell you more than the charm.",
"cups-12|swords-08":"An offer of romance reaches someone who feels bound by their own thinking; the invitation is real, but only your own willingness unties the blindfold.",
"cups-12|swords-09":"A romantic overture meets a mind that spirals after dark; the gesture is easier to read in daylight, once worry has loosened its hold.",
"cups-12|swords-10":"A new invitation follows something that ended completely; you can respond to the gesture honestly without pretending the old chapter did not matter.",
"cups-12|swords-11":"An eager invitation meets a careful watcher; asking real questions before saying yes is not coldness, it is how a sincere offer earns trust.",
"cups-12|swords-12":"Two fast movers collide, one led by feeling and one by argument; the romance goes smoother if the charge is slowed enough to hear the other person.",
"cups-12|swords-13":"A charming offer is read by someone who sees through comforting stories; sincerity survives that scrutiny, and flattery does not.",
"cups-12|swords-14":"The heart wants to say yes to the romantic gesture, and a fair-minded judgement asks whether the terms are honest; firm principle weighs the charm.",
"cups-12|pentacles-01":"Something concrete and workable arrives beside the romantic offer; if the feeling is real, it can be given a practical shape and an honest beginning.",
"cups-12|pentacles-02":"An invitation of the heart has to fit into a juggled life; the offer is more believable when someone makes real room for it in the week.",
"cups-12|pentacles-03":"Ordinary teamwork becomes the test of a romantic gesture; how it holds up while people do careful, useful work together says more than candlelight.",
"cups-12|pentacles-04":"An open-handed invitation meets a closed fist around security; the gesture invites you to loosen your grip, if only enough to see what is on offer.",
"cups-12|pentacles-05":"Someone feeling shut out and short of resources is offered romance; accept warmth with care, and let kindness be real before it is expected to fix things.",
"cups-12|pentacles-06":"A gesture of the heart works best inside fair give and take; an offer that asks nothing back is lovely, one that keeps score is not.",
"cups-12|pentacles-07":"An eager invitation meets a patient grower; step back and assess what has actually taken root, because the romance deserves time, not a rushed harvest.",
"cups-12|pentacles-08":"A romantic impulse meets the repeated, unglamorous hour; the gesture proves itself through practice and follow-through, not through the first charming moment.",
"cups-12|pentacles-09":"An invitation reaches someone who is whole and settled on their own; the offer is a choice, not a need, which is what makes it worth considering.",
"cups-12|pentacles-10":"Set against a life built to last, the romantic offer raises one question: can the gesture sit comfortably inside commitments that already matter?",
"cups-12|pentacles-11":"Both sides are earnest and both are learning, since romance meets a student of the practical; be kind about the clumsy attempts on either side.",
"cups-12|pentacles-12":"A charming invitation is matched with a slow, steady pace; the romance is built the same way as anything reliable, one dependable day at a time.",
"cups-12|pentacles-13":"An offer of romance meets practical, capable care; the sweetest gesture is the one that shows attention to how another person actually lives.",
"cups-12|pentacles-14":"A romantic invitation meets proven competence and provision; feeling and stability can complement each other if neither is asked to impress the other.",
