"cups-14|pentacles-11":"A mature heart meets an eager student; steady kindness gives a beginner the safety to try, fail, and keep going.",
"cups-14|pentacles-12":"Composed feeling meets dependable effort; emotional steadiness and reliable follow-through make a pair others lean on without ever thinking about it.",
"cups-14|pentacles-13":"Emotional command and practical care combine into a reliable kind of warmth; this is the person whose kindness shows up as real, capable help.",
"cups-14|pentacles-14":"Emotional maturity meets material mastery; a steady heart and a skilled hand make good stewards, provided each stays honest about its limits.",
"swords-01|swords-02":"A clear, cutting thought meets a standoff with eyes shut; one insight could end the stalemate, if you are willing to take the cover off and look.",
"swords-01|swords-03":"Naming the hurt plainly is what the clear thought is for; seeing the pain exactly as it is stings, yet it stops it from spreading into vague dread.",
"swords-01|swords-04":"Insight lands better when you let it settle; a sharp new understanding and a deliberate pause work as a pair, with rest letting the idea take shape.",
"swords-01|swords-05":"Clarity can be used to win or to understand, and the difference matters; a cutting truth wielded for victory leaves damage that honest seeing would have avoided.",
"swords-01|swords-06":"Seeing a situation clearly is what makes a calmer departure possible; once the truth is named, moving toward quieter water becomes a decision instead of a flight.",
"swords-01|swords-07":"Sharp thinking meets sneaky thinking, and the same intelligence can serve honesty or evasion; decide which you are using, and notice which is being used around you.",
"swords-01|swords-08":"A single clear thought is the blade that could cut through self-made binds; the ropes are looser than they feel, and seeing that is the first slice.",
"swords-01|swords-09":"Lucid thought is the antidote to a spiraling mind; when the worst-case story loops at night, one plainly stated fact can interrupt it.",
"swords-01|swords-10":"Clear sight and a finished ending work together: once you can say exactly what is over, there is nothing left to defend, and the next breath comes easier.",
"swords-01|swords-11":"A sharp insight is paired with watchful, curious questioning; the best use of a new idea is to test it gently before you swing it.",
"swords-01|swords-12":"A clear thought gets a fast, forceful carrier; the idea is good, but the delivery may land harder than you intend, so check your tone before you charge.",
"swords-01|swords-13":"Truth arrives, and someone is ready to look at it without flinching; unsentimental clarity is rare, and when two kinds meet, little stays hidden for long.",
"swords-01|swords-14":"A fresh insight meets principle and fair judgement; the idea gains weight when it is held to a standard, and the standard gains life from the idea.",
"swords-01|pentacles-01":"A clear idea meets a solid opening; this is a rare moment when thinking and material possibility line up, so decide, then act on something you can touch.",
"swords-01|pentacles-02":"A sharp thought cuts through a juggled week; naming what truly matters lets you drop one ball without guilt and keep the rest moving.",
"swords-01|pentacles-03":"A clear idea is tested against skilled hands and a capable team; good thinking becomes real only when others help build it properly.",
"swords-01|pentacles-04":"A new thought challenges a tight hold on security; clear sight can tell you whether the grip protects something valuable or only fear of change.",
"swords-01|pentacles-05":"Seeing plainly why things feel scarce is the beginning of a way out; a clear thought can show the doorway that worry has been hiding from view.",
"swords-01|pentacles-06":"Clarity about what is fair clears the way for honest exchange; once the terms are stated plainly, giving and receiving stop being a guessing game.",
"swords-01|pentacles-07":"A cutting insight arrives while you assess the long effort; look at the results as they are, and let what you see guide the next step.",
"swords-01|pentacles-08":"A flash of understanding meets steady practice; the idea matters, but only the repeated work will turn it into a skill you can rely on.",
"swords-01|pentacles-09":"Honest thinking examines a comfortable, self-made life; clarity asks what is truly yours and what you have simply grown used to, and both answers are useful.",
"swords-01|pentacles-10":"A sharp, fresh thought meets a long-established structure; the old foundation can take a clear question, and the question may make it stronger.",
"swords-01|pentacles-11":"A new idea falls into the hands of an eager learner; clear thinking is a skill that grows with study, so write the thought down and test it.",
"swords-01|pentacles-12":"A bright thought needs a patient carrier; the insight will only matter if someone follows through, steadily, on the unglamorous steps it requires.",
"swords-01|pentacles-13":"A clear mind meets practical care; the sharpest idea is the one that makes daily life work better for the people who depend on it.",
"swords-01|pentacles-14":"Sharp insight meets mastery of the material; knowing exactly what to do and having the means to do it is a strong position, provided it is used fairly.",
"swords-02|swords-03":"A stalemate kept in place by not looking may hide a hurt that needs a name; once the pain is stated plainly, the standoff can finally move.",
"swords-02|swords-04":"A deadlock and a need for rest are close relatives; stepping back from an unsolvable standoff may be the only way to see it with fresh eyes.",
