"swords-03|swords-11":"Hurt meets a watchful, questioning mind; asking what actually happened, rather than what you fear happened, softens the wound by replacing guesses with facts.",
"swords-03|swords-12":"A sore spot meets a blunt, rushing force; speed and bluntness can reopen the wound, so choose words slowly when the subject is tender.",
"swords-03|swords-13":"Sorrow meets unsparing clarity; the hurt is acknowledged without cushioning, and while that stings, it also stops you from living inside a gentler fiction.",
"swords-03|swords-14":"Heartache meets fair judgement; a measured, principled look at what happened lets you grieve without handing down a verdict you will regret.",
"swords-03|pentacles-01":"A wound meets something solid and new; the opening does not erase the hurt, but it gives you somewhere practical to stand while it heals.",
"swords-03|pentacles-02":"Sorrow meets a busy, juggled life; keeping everything moving can postpone the ache, so leave one small gap in the day to feel what is there.",
"swords-03|pentacles-03":"Pain meets people who work well together; being useful alongside others is a quiet comfort, and a team can carry you while the heart mends.",
"swords-03|pentacles-04":"Hurt makes a person clutch what feels safe; understand the impulse, but notice whether the guarded stance is protecting you or keeping the wound open.",
"swords-03|pentacles-05":"Heartache meets the cold of lack; two kinds of feeling left out arrive together, and reaching toward warmth, even a little, is the practical answer.",
"swords-03|pentacles-06":"A hurt meets give and take; being offered help, or offering it, is how a wound begins to close, so allow yourself to be on either side.",
