"swords-03|pentacles-08":"Sorrow meets steady, repeated work; the daily practice of a craft can hold you steady while grief runs its course.",
"swords-03|pentacles-09":"A named hurt meets a self-made refuge; a quiet, comfortable space of your own is a legitimate place to mend, not a way of hiding.",
"swords-03|pentacles-10":"Heartache meets something built to last; the wound matters, and so does the larger life around it, which remains steady while the sore place heals.",
"swords-03|pentacles-11":"A raw hurt meets a gentle learner; treat the healing like a new skill, with patience, small steps, and no expectation of getting it perfect.",
"swords-03|pentacles-12":"Sorrow meets slow, steady effort; reliable routines may not feel like they are touching the pain, but they carry you across the hardest stretch.",
"swords-03|pentacles-13":"A hurt meets practical, capable care; being looked after in ordinary ways, with food, order, and company, is one of the oldest forms of healing.",
"swords-03|pentacles-14":"Heartache meets calm competence and security; a stable life does not remove the ache, but it gives sorrow somewhere safe to be felt.",
