"swords-07|pentacles-06":"A fair exchange is the honest alternative to taking quietly: when both sides give and receive in the open, nobody needs a clever workaround.",
"swords-07|pentacles-07":"Strategy and patience share a root: both ask you to think about the long harvest, and both fail if you grab at the crop too early.",
"swords-07|pentacles-08":"Quiet cleverness is no match for long practice, and the person who simply puts in the hours tends to outlast the one hunting shortcuts.",
