"swords-07|pentacles-10":"Anything meant to last needs honest foundations, so a clever shortcut that undermines trust will weaken the structure you hope to leave behind.",
"swords-07|pentacles-11":"A beginner hunting for the fast route learns the real lesson: study the craft properly, because the quick trick usually costs more than it saves.",
"swords-07|pentacles-12":"Slow and reliable work puts crafty maneuvering to shame, and the steady one is trusted precisely because no hidden agenda sits behind the effort.",
"swords-07|pentacles-13":"Practical warmth is the opposite of scheming: a capable, caring hand looks after what is real and has no need for cunning.",
"swords-07|pentacles-14":"Mastery earns what a quiet scheme only tries to grab, and a secure provider's confidence shows in how openly they handle things.",
"swords-08|swords-09":"Being trapped by your own story and lying awake with dread are two faces of one loop, and naming the thought loosens both.",
"swords-08|swords-10":"A fully finished chapter and a self-imposed trap both loosen the same way: stop retelling the story that says there is no way out.",
"swords-08|swords-11":"A questioning, watchful mind is the key to the blindfold, because asking whether your assumptions are true can show that the ropes are loose.",
"swords-08|swords-12":"Feeling stuck and charging ahead are opposites, and the answer lies between them: act, but on a clear look at what is actually holding you.",
